7": "$2$", "MATH_0038": "$2$", "MATH_0039": "$2$", "MATH_0040": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-ameliorate-morphism-categories-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-equivalence-2-fibre-product}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-equivalence-fibred-categories}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-ameliorate-morphism-categories-fibred-groupoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e33b96ec733fe479c989f839cf6aa916d5d828332ee18b94c4f55ad05b35f055", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2b37e24776000075398f2d16f133f2fc7e617bf3e9f1e7db24bf73e2cb96928", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will show that both <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003>\nare equivalent to the category fibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0004>\nover <MATH_0005>, see proof of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nChoose a quasi-inverse <MATH_0006> in the\n<MATH_0007>-category of categories over <MATH_0008>.\nSince the right triangle of the diagram is <MATH_0009>-commutative we see that\n<MATH_0010>\nis <MATH_0011>-commutative. Hence we obtain a <MATH_0012>-morphism\n<MATH_0013>\nby the universal property of the <MATH_0014>-fibre product. Moreover <MATH_0015>\nis a morphism of categories over <MATH_0016> (!) and an equivalence\n(by the assumption that <MATH_0017> is an equivalence, see\nLemma <REF_0002>).\nHence <MATH_0018> is an equivalence in the <MATH_0019>-category of categories fibred\nin groupoids over <MATH_0020> by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nWe still have to construct a <MATH_0021>-isomorphism between <MATH_0022> and\nthe functor <MATH_0023>,\n<MATH_0024>\nconstructed in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0025> and <MATH_0026>\nbe <MATH_0027>-isomorphisms between <MATH_0028>-morphisms of categories over <MATH_0029>.\nNote that <MATH_0030> is given by the rule\n<MATH_0031>\non objects. Then we see that\n<MATH_0032>\nis a functorial isomorphism which gives our <MATH_0033>-morphism\n<MATH_0034>. Finally, if the diagram commutes then\n<MATH_0035> is the identity for all <MATH_0036> and we see that this\n<MATH_0037>-morphism is a <MATH_0038>-morphism in the <MATH_0039>-category of categories\nover <MATH_0040>.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bd1d5e6af50ed37a0874e14b6a6b4ed31e1dfc96530c2a2b93edf5f425d1f554", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:06N8:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:19558970d065ffffbccb7f35bc3819fa7ec52538f5b7487392ae8f22b69d890f", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p013-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:24d263438465ff0eb35fe7a3a4090d91fabfc03a3fff2a63ec6bb3456ce70762"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": [], "policy_revision": "git:b33b9b37f1623d49d4030a11f1661dfc29fa2ce4", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:06N8:proof/0001", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:02XU:paragraph/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [], "unit_id": "tag:02XU:title"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_required_terms": {"catalog_hash": "sha256:899a668e50f3487b37dd8781e9b5a88e3e16d272ad91b4078ac6b9d847935c12", "occurrences": [{"concept": "presheaf", "projection_end": 10, "projection_start": 0, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "Presheaves"}, {"concept": "category", "projection_end": 24, "projection_start": 14, "rule": "catalog", "source_term": "categories"}], "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88452e9a936f3f114bb7834e2bd56f16d9a28519a8bd76e41a5054f2cbbb247d", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1d293550f7dce49124a84b8ba4f6e32483fa79ff503934877946d91a958d97c7", "unit_id": "tag:02XU:title"}, "style_guide_path": "config/style-guide.md", "turn_id":